    "lastText": "The spreadsheet engine from TASK.md is built, and all 80 tests pass with `npm test`. The work is committed as \"Implement minisheet engine\".\n\n- **Engine:** `src/sheet.js` exports `Sheet` with `set`, `get` and `getInput`. It covers the operators, coercion rules, errors, circular-reference handling and every function listed in the spec. Changing a cell updates everything that depends on it, and a 9,000-cell dependency chain evaluates without stack overflow.\n- **Tests:** `test/sheet.test.js` covers literals, operators, each function family, errors, cycles and recalculation.\n- **README:** `README.md` lists every supported function.\n\nWhere the spec was silent I made these calls:\n- **`COUNTBLANK`:** it counts only truly empty cells, so a formula returning `\"\"` is not counted.\n- **`INDEX`:** it follows the spec literally, so `INDEX(A1:C1, 2)` on a one-row range gives `#REF!`, whereas Excel would return `B1`.\n- **`PRODUCT`:** with no numbers it returns 0.",
